,"month":12,"modis_raw":105,"viirs_raw":537,"harmonized":478}]}],"seams":[{"id":"modis_to_snpp_2012","label":"MODIS → Suomi NPP transition, 2009–2011 vs 2012–2014","ratio_harmonized":0.972,"ratio_naive":3.801},{"id":"snpp_to_n20_2026","label":"Suomi NPP → NOAA-20 transition, checked on 2024–2025","ratio_harmonized":1.001,"ratio_naive":0.984}],"limitations":["Small fires that VIIRS (375 m) sees and MODIS (1 km) does not are recovered before 2012 only statistically: the coefficient carries over the average ratio, not individual events.","In small areas (smaller than a 1° cell) the coefficient is taken from the cell or the 5° block — the estimate is coarser and the interval wider.","2000–2002: Terra only, one morning overpass — the error is 1.7–2.1 times higher than for Terra + Aqua, and in 2003–2011 the Terra-only estimate runs about 3 % below the Terra + Aqua one.","Days when the lead satellite did not report are filled from another one (NOAA-20 for Suomi NPP, Terra for Aqua); Terra outages in 2000–2012 cannot be filled, so those months are flagged as sensor gaps and may be understated.","Active lava flows and gas flares: MODIS and VIIRS classify them differently, so such places are masked for all satellites and their coefficient comes from the surrounding 5° block; detections left there are less reliable."]}